---
import { DOCS_PATH } from "../../site.config.ts";
// Spec Part 4 item 19: what a customer can see on-chain. docs/security says the same.
---

<section id="privacy" class="section" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="privacy-title" class="section__title">Privacy, honestly</h2>
    <p class="section__lede">
      Every customer can look up their own payment on a block explorer. What else they can see depends on the mode you
      run.
    </p>

    <div class="privacy">
      <article class="privacy__card" aria-labelledby="privacy-watch">
        <h3 id="privacy-watch" class="privacy__title">Watch mode</h3>
        <dl class="privacy__list">
          <div class="privacy__item privacy__item--yes">
            <dt>Hidden</dt>
            <dd>
              Each invoice gets a fresh address from your wallet, so a customer never sees one address that holds all your
              payments.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div class="privacy__item privacy__item--no">
            <dt>Not hidden</dt>
            <dd>
              Payments land straight in your wallet. When you spend, your wallet merges inputs, so a customer who follows
              their coins can see the other payments spent with them.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div class="privacy__item privacy__item--no">
            <dt>No private hop</dt>
            <dd>
              The trail above needs privacy routing, and privacy routing needs routed mode. Watch-mode coins are never
              routed, because the Worker holds no key for them.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </article>

      <article class="privacy__card" aria-labelledby="privacy-routed">
        <h3 id="privacy-routed" class="privacy__title">Routed mode</h3>
        <p class="privacy__text">
          Deposits are swept to one hot wallet per chain (EVM forwarders, Tron, Solana), and UTXO spends merge inputs. So
          a customer who follows their own payment can see the hot wallet and other deposits until privacy routing moves
          the funds.
        </p>
        <p class="privacy__text privacy__text--strong">Privacy routing reduces this. It does not remove it.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="section__more">
      <a href={`${DOCS_PATH}security/`}>Read the security notes</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
